# T-1066 param substitution: a zero-param structural alias declared with a record body.
# BoxRecord: [type [let a] [id: a]] has one param `a`, body [id: a].
# After param substitution with Int, body becomes [id: Int] — a concrete record type.
# body_contains_tycon_ref([id: a]) = false (no TyCon refs, only a param TypeVar),
# so after substitution the expanded body is a plain record type.
#
# At runtime: BoxRecord TypeAlias is skipped (named-key body, no constructor injection).
# Only `f` and `result` appear in the dict output.
#
# At typecheck: no warnings — structural alias with one param, clean annotation site.
[
  BoxRecord: [type [let a] [id: a]]
  f: [fn [let x] x.id]
  result: [f [id: 42]]
]
=== out
Dict({"f": Function(x), "result": Int(42)})
